se Rodriguez Sevilla, Fundació de Recerca Clínic Barcelona-Institut d’Investigacions Biomèdiques August Pi i Sunyer (IDIBAPS), Spain\nTopic: Decoding Multi-Lineage Evolutionary Trajectories in Lymphoma Patients under Adoptive Cell Therapies\nTopics-in-Focus Junior Research Grant\nHemoglobinopathies\nOyindamola Adebayo, KU Leuven, Belgium\nTopic: Elucidation of the underlying mechanism of Apolipoprotein L1-mediated sickle cell nephropathy\nPrecision Hematology\nManuel Mataix, Centro de Investigaciones Energéticas Medioambientales y Tecnológicas (CIEMAT) - Instituto de Investigación Sanitaria Fundación Jiménez Díaz (IIS-FJD), Spain\nTopic: Novel non-viral delivery approaches for in vivo targeting of Fanconi anemia hematopoietic stem and progenitor cell\nBilateral Collaborative Grant\nMiguel Ganuza, Queen Mary University of London, United Kingdom\nCatherine Sawai, Bordeaux Institute of Oncology, France\nTopic: m6A RNA methylation and METTL3 at the interface of inflammation and clonal hematopoiesis\nThomas Fox, University College London, United Kingdom\nRoman Jerala, National Institute of Chemistry, Slovenia\nTopic: Epitope editing coupled with a novel lipid nanoparticle platform to facilitate the generation of in vivo cell therapies.\nInnovation Grant\nAlessandro Casini, Geneva University Hospitals, Switzerland\nGiancarlo Castaman, Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria Careggi Florence, Italy\nSaskia Schols, Radboud University Medical Centre, The Netherlands\nTomas Simurda, Martin and University Hospital, Slovakia\nMaartje van den Biggelaar, Amsterdam University Medical Center, The Netherlands\nTopic: Multi-omics in hereditary fibrinogen disorders: bridging the genotype-phenotype gap\nHind Medyouf, RWTH University Hospital Aachen, Germany\nAlessandra Giorgetti, IDIBELL, Spain\nEster Mejstrikova, Charles University, Czechia\nMarcelo Szymanski de Toledo, RWTH University Hospital Aachen, Germany\nRiccardo Masetti, IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria di Bologna, Italy\nTopic: GErmline Mutations and Interactions in the Niche of Inherited GATA2 predisposition syndrome (GEMINI)\nResearch Mobility Grant\nAimilia Vareli, Brighton and Sussex Medical School, United Kingdom\nTopic: Disentangling NF-κΒ and BCL2 in Diffuse Large B-cell Lymphoma\nFederica Bruno, Imperial College London, United Kingdom\nTopic: Understanding long term effects of strong inflammation on HSCs\nMartina Failla, University of Milano-Bicocca, Italy\nTopic: Fructose-induced Metabolic Vulnerabilities in Bone Marrow and Extramedullary Disease in IDH2-Mutant Acute Myeloid Leukemia\nMartina Mia Mitic, Institute of Molecular Genetics and Genetic Engineering, University of Belgrade, Serbia\nTopic: Synthesis and characterization of recombinant STAB2 protein variants associated with venous thromboembolism\nIvan Ferrari, Humanitas University, Italy\nTopic: Functional validation of clonal evolution patterns in myelodysplastic syndromes using bone marrow organoid models\nMatus Kolarik, Second faculty of Medicine, Charles University, Czechia\nTopic: Chaperone mediated autophagy as a potential regulator of redox defense in ALL\nTamás Jónás Laufer, University College London, United Kingdom\nTopic: CRISISS – Optimization of a CRISPR‑based Inducible Safety Switch for Cell and Gene Therapies\nMandy Raum, Institute of Cell Biology and Immunology Thurgau (BITG), Switzerland\nTopic: In vivo erythropoiesis in the WHIM mouse model\nSelma Sorri, University of Helsinki, Finland\nTopic: DTX1 mutations in large B-cell lymphoma pathogenesis\nIan Márquez López, Fundació de Recerca Clínic Barcelona-Institut d’Investigacions Biomèdiques August Pi i Sunyer, Spain\nTopic: TRACE-FL: Topographic Reconstruction of Archetypes and Clonal Evolution in Follicular Lymphoma\nCarlos López Pleguezuelos, Fundació de Recerca Clínic Barcelona-Institut d’Investigacions Biomèdiques August Pi i Sunyer, Spain\nTopic: Epigenetic clonal tracing: origin, proliferation and evolutionary dynamics of CLL at single-cell resolut